Compensation of notaries.-No notary public shall -charge or receive for any service rendered by
him any fee, remuneration, or compensation except as expressly prescribed in the following schedule:
For protests of drafts, bills of exchange, or promissory notes for non-acceptance or non-payment, and for
notice thereof, three pesos;
For the registration of such protest and filing or safekeeping of same, one peso and fifty centavos;
For authenticating powers of attorney, one peso and fifty centavos;
For sworn statement concerning correctness of any account or other document, one peso;
For each oath or affirmation, eighty centavos;

For receiving evidence of indebtedness to be sent outside, one peso and fifty centavos;
For issuing a certified copy from his register and attesting its correctness, two pesos;
For issuing a certified copy of all or part of his notarial records or receive depositions, for each one hundred
words, thirty centavos;
For acknowledging other documents not enumerated in this section, one peso and fifty centavos: Provided,
however, That the total amount which a notary may charge for the acknowledgment of a document shall in no
case exceed five pesos and fifty centavos.
